{
    "background_story": "Jonah was a brilliant and reclusive mathematician who spent his life studying the mysteries of the universe. He became obsessed with the concept of infinitude, pouring over theories and equations that attempted to grasp the infinite nature of space and time. As he delved deeper into his research, Jonah began to see the world as a vast, intricate web of endless possibilities. He became convinced that every decision, every event, and every thought was connected to an infinite number of parallel universes. Jonah's work took him to the edges of human understanding, and he often lost himself in the infinite expanse of his own mind. Despite the isolation, he felt a sense of freedom in the infinitude, as if the boundaries of reality no longer constrained him. His groundbreaking theories on infinite sets and fractals earned him a reputation as a visionary, but Jonah knew that he had only scratched the surface of the infinite mysteries that lay before him.",
